  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_16. Let triangle JKL be a right triangle with sides JK = 8, KL = 6. Let triangle MNO be a right triangle with sides MN = 12. Triangle JKL is similar to triangle MNO by AA similarity (congruent angle pairs: J \u2245 M, K \u2245 N). Find the length of NO in MNO.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A surveyor is measuring two similar right triangles formed by sight lines and landmarks. In the first triangle JKL, the two legs measure JK = 8 and KL = 6, meeting at a right angle at K. The surveyor then identifies a second similar right triangle MNO, where the right angle is at N, and one leg measures MN = 12.\n\nThe surveyor knows that triangle JKL is similar to triangle MNO because angle J is congruent to angle M and angle K is congruent to angle N (by AA similarity). To complete her survey, she needs to find the length of side NO in triangle MNO.\n\nWhat is the length of NO?"
}